A note on what is *not* published
---------------------------------

The corpus lists endpoint URLs that were already public in the Model Context Protocol
registry, so publishing them adds no exposure. Per-endpoint verdicts are released only
after the disclosure window described in `docs/ETHICS.md` §9 has closed, and no endpoint is
named as an example of a failure without its operator having been notified first.

Personal data encountered incidentally in fetched documents (contact addresses, provider
names in agent cards or authorization-server metadata) is masked before publication. It was
never sought; see `docs/ETHICS.md` §8.

Hosts that asked to be excluded are in `docs/opt-out.txt`. They are absent from the corpus
and from every denominator.
